1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,060
you

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,060
you

3
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:41,710
Krishnamurti in dialogue with Dr. Alan

4
00:00:41,710 --> 00:00:45,360
W. Anderson. J. Krishnamurti was born in

5
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:48,400
South India and educated in England. For the past

6
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:51,440
40 years he has been speaking in the United

7
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:54,700
States, Europe, India, Australia, and other parts of

8
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:57,960
the world. From the outset of his life's work,

9
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:00,840
he repudiated all connections with organized religions

10
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:03,720
and ideologies and said that his only

11
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:07,620
concern was to set men absolutely unconditionally free.

12
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:11,520
He is the author of many books, among them

13
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:14,880
The Awakening of Intelligence, The Urgency of

14
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:18,240
Change, Freedom from the Known, and The Flight

15
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:21,840
of the Eagle. This is one of a series

16
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:25,440
of dialogues between Krishnamurti and Dr. Alan W. Anderson,

17
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:28,099
who is professor of religious studies at

18
00:01:28,099 --> 00:01:30,759
San Diego State University where he teaches Indian

19
00:01:30,759 --> 00:01:33,619
and Chinese scriptures and the oracular

20
00:01:33,619 --> 00:01:36,480
tradition. Dr. Anderson, a published poet,

21
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:39,580
received his degree from Columbia University and

22
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:42,680
the Union Theological Seminary. He has been

23
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:44,880
honored with a Distinguished Teaching

24
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:47,080
Award from the California State Universities.

25
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:56,840
Mr. Krishnamurti, I was wonderfully overjoyed in

26
00:01:56,840 --> 00:02:06,600
our last conversation. For myself, just as

27
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:11,420
as one who was trying in listening to you

28
00:02:11,420 --> 00:02:16,240
to learn something of his inwardness, to follow along the

29
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:20,540
passage that we had made from fear through the

30
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:24,840
points as we moved until we came to pleasure,

31
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:30,300
and as we left off we were still talking of

32
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:35,760
pleasure. And I hope we can begin now to move along.

33
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:41,660
We were saying, sir, weren't we,

34
00:02:41,660 --> 00:02:47,560
pleasure, enjoyment, delight, and joy and happiness.

35
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:56,020
And what relationship has pleasure with enjoyment

36
00:02:56,020 --> 00:03:04,480
and with joy, with happiness? Is pleasure happiness?

37
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:10,859
Is pleasure joy? Is pleasure enjoyment? Or

38
00:03:10,859 --> 00:03:17,239
is pleasure something entirely different from those two?

39
00:03:17,239 --> 00:03:22,779
A. In English we think we make

40
00:03:22,779 --> 00:03:28,320
a distinction between pleasure and joy without necessarily

41
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:33,960
knowing what we mean. In our use, in

42
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:38,760
our employment of the words, we will discriminate sometimes.

43
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:42,100
We think it odd to use the word pleasure

44
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:45,440
rather than joy when we think that joy is appropriate.

45
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:49,800
The relation between the word please and pleasure interests

46
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:54,160
me very much. We will say to a person,

47
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,899
please sit down, and usually

48
00:03:56,899 --> 00:03:58,799
that would be thought of as...

49
00:03:58,799 --> 00:04:00,359
K. Have the pleasure to sit down.

50
00:04:00,359 --> 00:04:01,720
A. Yes. It's not a request.

51
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:03,320
K. Please yourself to sit down.

52
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:05,040
A. It's an invitation, not a request.

53
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:06,000
K. Not quite.

54
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,280
A. Be pleased to sit down.

55
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:10,840
K. Be pleased to sit down.

56
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:13,840
A. It's be pleased to be seated.

57
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:14,760
K. Yes.

58
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:16,560
K. Like in Italian, French, so on.

59
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:21,920
A. Right. So within pleasure itself, the

60
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:27,280
word pleasure, there's the intimation of joy,

61
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:29,740
intimation of it that is

62
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:32,200
not strictly reduced to the word.

63
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:38,100
K. I would like to question

64
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:44,000
whether pleasure has any relationship with joy.

65
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,200
A. Pleasure.

66
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:47,920
A. Not in itself, I take it, you mean.

67
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:52,520
K. Or even beyond the word.

68
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:55,900
Is there a line or

69
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:59,280
a continuity of pleasure to joy?

70
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:03,280
Is there a connecting link?

71
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:10,640
Because what is pleasure?

72
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:16,400
I take pleasure in eating, I take pleasure in walking,

73
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:20,640
I take pleasure in accumulating money,

74
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:24,599
I take pleasure in a dozen, dozen, dozen things,

75
00:05:24,599 --> 00:05:33,280
sex, hurting people, sadistic instincts, violent.

76
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:36,919
They are all forms of a pleasure.

77
00:05:36,919 --> 00:05:39,560
I enjoy. I won't use the word enjoy.

78
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:48,600
I take pleasure in and pursue that pleasure.

79
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:57,440
One wants to hurt people,

80
00:05:57,440 --> 00:06:00,600
and that gives great pleasure.

81
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:03,480
One wants to have power.

82
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:06,280
It doesn't matter whether you cook, or the wife,

83
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:11,320
or a thousand people, it's the same.

84
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:16,520
The pleasure in something which is sustained,

85
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:23,520
nourished, kept going.

86
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:27,479
And this pleasure, when it is thwarted,

87
00:06:27,479 --> 00:06:33,440
becomes violent, anger, jealousy, fury,

88
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:36,040
wanting to break,

89
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:41,040
all kinds of neurotic activities, and so on, so on.

90
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:45,540
So, what is pleasure, and what

91
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:50,040
is it that keeps it going?

92
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:54,780
What is the pursuit of

93
00:06:54,780 --> 00:06:58,280
it, the constant direction of it?

94
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:03,780
I think, I think, something

95
00:07:03,780 --> 00:07:08,280
in our first or second conversation,

96
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:11,280
I think it was the first, is intimated here,

97
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:17,280
when we talked about the built-in necessity

98
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:26,280
that one observes in a progress

99
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:34,280
that is never consummated.

100
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:37,280
It's just nothing but a

101
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:40,280
termination and then a new start,

102
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:46,280
but no consummation at all, no totality,

103
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:51,280
no fulfilment, feeling full is what I mean by that.

104
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:56,780
Yes, I understand, sir, but

105
00:07:56,780 --> 00:08:02,280
what is it that's called pleasure?

106
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:07,280
I see something, something which I enjoy,

107
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:12,280
and I want it, pleasure, pleasure and possession.

108
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:17,280
Take that simple thing, which the child, the grown-up man,

109
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:21,280
the priest, they all have

110
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:25,280
this feeling of pleasure in possession.

111
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:31,280
A toy, or a house, or possessing knowledge,

112
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:35,280
or possessing the idea of God,

113
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:39,280
or the pleasure the dictators have,

114
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:46,280
the totalitarian brutalities, the pleasure.

115
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:48,280
What is that pleasure?

116
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:55,280
To make it very, very simple, what is that pleasure?

117
00:08:55,280 --> 00:09:00,280
Look, sir, what happens?

118
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:05,280
There is a single tree on the hill,

119
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:09,280
green meadow, deer,

120
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:15,280
and there is this single tree standing on the hill.

121
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:20,280
You see that and you say, how marvellous.

122
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:23,280
Not verbally, merely you say, how marvellous,

123
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:25,280
to communicate to somebody,

124
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:27,280
but when you are by yourself and see that,

125
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:31,280
it is really astonishingly beautiful.

126
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:34,280
The whole movement of the earth, the flowers,

127
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:36,280
the deer, the meadows, the water,

128
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:41,280
and the single tree with the shadow.

129
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:44,280
You see that.

130
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:49,280
It is almost breathtaking.

131
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:54,280
And you turn away and go away.

132
00:09:54,280 --> 00:10:00,280
Then thought says, how extraordinary that was.

133
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:02,280
A. Compared with what now is.

134
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:04,280
K. How extraordinary.

135
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:08,280
I must have it again.

136
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:13,280
I must get that same feeling which I had then,

137
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:18,280
for two seconds or five minutes.

138
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:23,280
So thought, see what has taken place.

139
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:28,280
There was immediate response to that beauty,

140
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:34,280
non-verbal, non-emotional, non-sentimental, non-romantic.

141
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:38,280
Then thought comes along and says,

142
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:42,280
how extraordinary, what a delight that was.

143
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:47,280
And then the memory of it, and the repetition,

144
00:10:47,280 --> 00:10:52,280
the demand, the desire for the repetition.

145
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:57,280
A. When we go to performances,

146
00:10:57,280 --> 00:11:00,280
this happens with what we call the encore, doesn't it?

147
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:02,280
K. Encore.

148
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:05,280
A. And with encores there is a creeping embarrassment,

149
00:11:05,280 --> 00:11:07,280
because with the first reappearance

150
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:11,280
– well, this is a sign of adulation, praise,

151
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:13,280
and everybody is happy.

152
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:16,280
But then of course there is the problem of

153
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:19,280
how many more encores can be made,

154
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:20,780
and maybe the last encore is a

155
00:11:20,780 --> 00:11:22,280
signal that we are fed up now,

156
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:25,280
we don't want any more.

157
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:29,280
Yes, I understand, I think I am following you.

158
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:39,280
K. So thought gives nourishment, sustains it,

159
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:45,280
and gives it a direction to pleasure.

160
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:52,280
There was no pleasure at the moment of perception

161
00:11:52,280 --> 00:11:54,780
of that tree, the hill,

162
00:11:54,780 --> 00:11:57,280
the shadows, the deer, the water,

163
00:11:57,280 --> 00:12:01,280
the meadow, the whole thing was astonishing.

164
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:09,280
That was real, non-verbal, non-romantic and so on.

165
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:12,280
Perception.

166
00:12:14,280 --> 00:12:16,780
It has nothing to do with

167
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:19,280
me or you, it was there.

168
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:24,280
Then thought comes along and says, memory of it,

169
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:28,280
continuing that memory tomorrow,

170
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:33,280
and the demand for that, and the pursuit of that.

171
00:12:33,280 --> 00:12:35,780
And when I come back to

172
00:12:35,780 --> 00:12:38,280
it tomorrow, it is not the same.

173
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:43,280
I feel a little bit shocked, a little bit...

174
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:45,780
I was inspired, now I must

175
00:12:45,780 --> 00:12:48,280
find means of getting again inspired,

176
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:52,280
therefore I take a drink, women, this or that.

177
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:53,280
You follow?

178
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:55,280
A. Oh, yes, yes, yes.

179
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:58,280
Do you think in the history of culture

180
00:12:58,280 --> 00:13:00,780
the establishment of festivals would be

181
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:03,280
related to what you are saying?

182
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:05,280
K. Of course, it is the whole thing, sir.

183
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:08,280
A. We live for...

184
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:14,280
In English we have this saying, to live it up.

185
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:17,280
The rest of the time we are living it down.

186
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:19,780
K. Down, yes. Mardi Gras, you

187
00:13:19,780 --> 00:13:22,280
know, the whole business of it.

188
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:26,280
So there it is. I see that.

189
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:28,280
See what it is, sir.

190
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:33,280
Pleasure is sustained by thought.

191
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:42,280
Sexual pleasure, the image, the thinking over it, all that,

192
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:46,280
and the repetition of it,

193
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:48,780
and the pleasure of it, and

194
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:51,280
go on, keep on, keep on, routine.

195
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:58,280
Now, what a relationship,

196
00:13:58,280 --> 00:14:02,280
what is the place of pleasure or relationship

197
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:07,280
to the delight of the moment?

198
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:13,280
Not even a delight, it is something inexpressible.

199
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:21,280
So is there any relationship between pleasure and enjoyment?

200
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:26,280
Enjoyment becomes pleasure when thought says,

201
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:31,280
I have enjoyed it, I must have more of it.

202
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:38,280
A. It is actually a falling out of joy.

203
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:40,280
K. Yes, that is it.

204
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:46,280
You see, sir, so pleasure has no relationship

205
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:51,280
to ecstasy, to delight, to enjoyment,

206
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:54,280
or to joy and happiness.

207
00:14:54,280 --> 00:15:05,280
Because pleasure is the movement of thought in direction.

208
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:09,280
It doesn't matter what direction, but in a direction.

209
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:14,280
The others have no direction.

210
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:18,280
Pleasure and enjoyment, you enjoy.

211
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:21,280
Joy is something you cannot invite,

212
00:15:21,280 --> 00:15:23,280
happiness you cannot invite,

213
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:24,780
it happens and you don't know

214
00:15:24,780 --> 00:15:26,280
if you are happy at that moment.

215
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:28,780
It is only the next moment

216
00:15:28,780 --> 00:15:31,280
you say, how marvellous that was.

217
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:34,280
So, see what takes place.

218
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:38,280
Can the mind, the brain,

219
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:43,280
register the beauty of that hill and tree

220
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:50,280
and the water and the meadows, and end it?

221
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:56,280
Not say, I want it again.

222
00:15:57,280 --> 00:16:03,280
A. Yes. This would take us back to that,

223
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:06,280
what you have just said now,

224
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:08,280
would take us back to that word negation

225
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:10,280
that we spoke of before.

226
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:13,280
Because there has to be a moment

227
00:16:13,280 --> 00:16:16,280
when we are about to fall out.

228
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:18,280
We are about to fall out.

229
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:21,280
And what you are saying is,

230
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:25,280
the moment that about to fall out appears,

231
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:28,280
something must be done.

232
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:31,280
K. You will see it in a minute, sir.

233
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:35,280
You will see what extraordinary things take place.

234
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:42,280
I see pleasure, enjoyment, joy and happiness.

235
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:45,280
See pleasure has not related to any of that,

236
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:49,280
the other two, joy and enjoyment.

237
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:57,280
So thought gives direction and sustains pleasure.

238
00:16:57,280 --> 00:17:01,280
Right. Now, I ask myself, mind asks,

239
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:08,280
can there be non-interference of thought,

240
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:16,280
non-interference of thought in pleasure?

241
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:20,280
I enjoy.

242
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:24,280
Why should thought come into it at all?

243
00:17:24,280 --> 00:17:26,280
A. There is no reason at all.

244
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:28,280
K. But it does. A. It does.

245
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:31,280
Now, the question arises,

246
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:34,280
how is the mind, the brain,

247
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:39,682
to stop thought entering into that enjoyment?

248
00:17:39,682 --> 00:17:40,182
路 murderer

249
00:17:40,642 --> 00:17:44,282
Not to interfere.

250
00:17:46,482 --> 00:17:48,482
Therefore they said,

251
00:17:48,482 --> 00:17:52,602
the ancients and the religious people,

252
00:17:52,602 --> 00:17:55,282
control thought.

253
00:17:55,282 --> 00:18:00,282
You follow? Don't let it creep in.

254
00:18:01,122 --> 00:18:03,202
Therefore control it.

255
00:18:03,202 --> 00:18:05,282
A minute it raises its ugly head,

256
00:18:05,282 --> 00:18:06,882
whack it off.

257
00:18:06,882 --> 00:18:08,402
It's like a hydra.

258
00:18:08,402 --> 00:18:10,282
It keeps on growing.

259
00:18:10,282 --> 00:18:12,282
Now,

260
00:18:14,482 --> 00:18:17,482
is it possible

261
00:18:18,122 --> 00:18:20,482
to enjoy,

262
00:18:20,482 --> 00:18:25,282
to take a delight in that lovely scene

263
00:18:25,282 --> 00:18:29,042
and not thought creeping in?

264
00:18:29,042 --> 00:18:32,042
Is this possible?

265
00:18:33,442 --> 00:18:36,042
I'll show you. It is possible,

266
00:18:36,042 --> 00:18:38,962
completely possible,

267
00:18:38,962 --> 00:18:42,161
if you are attentive at that moment,

268
00:18:42,161 --> 00:18:45,601
completely attentive.

